          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            can be flattened, by ignoring higher morphisms, into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ho(C)
            called its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
            %em triangulated structure
            is designed to capture the additional structure canonically existing on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ho(C)
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has the property of being
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+functor"} suspension functor
            = succeed "," do
              %em distinguished triangles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} shadows
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofibre+sequence"} homotopy (co)fibre sequences
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} stable (infinity,1)-categories
          %p
            A central class of examples of triangulated categories are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+categories"} derived categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(\mathcal{A})
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy categories
            of the stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories+of+chain+complexes"} (∞,1)-categories of chain complexes
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (infinity,1)-category of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} stable (infinity,1)-categories
            (though examples of “exotic” triangulated categories probably exist).
          %p
            By construction, passing from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            represents a serious loss of information. In practice, endowing the homotopy category with a triangulated structure is often sufficient for many purposes. However, as soon as one needs to remember the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            that existed in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
            in a triangulated category is not functorial. Hence it is often necessary to work with some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+triangulated+category"} enhanced
            notion of triangulated category, like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+derivators"} stable derivators
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretriangulated+dg-categories"} pretriangulated dg-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+categories"} stable model categories
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} stable (infinity,1)-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+triangulated+category"} enhanced triangulated category
            for more details.
          %h2#history History
          %p
            The notion of triangulated category was developed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Verdier"} Jean-Louis Verdier
            in his 1963 thesis under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandre+Grothendieck"} Alexandre Grothendieck
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albrecht+Dold"} Albrecht Dold
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+Puppe"} Dieter Puppe
            in a 1961 paper. A notable difference is that Dold-Puppe did not impose the octahedral axiom (TR4).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The traditional definition of
            %em triangulated category
            is the following. But see remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RedundancyInDefinition"}
            below.
          #TriangulatedCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong triangulated category
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+translation"}> with (additive) translation
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  equipped with a collection of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+translation"} triangles
                  called
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distinguished+triangles"} distinguished triangles
                  (dts)
              %li
                %p such that the following axioms hold
            %p
              %strong TR0:
              every triangle isomorphic to a distinguished triangle is itself a distinguished triangle;
            %p
              %strong TR1:
              the triangle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi X
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{Id_X}{\to} X \to 0 \to T X
            %p is a distinguished triangle;
            %p
              %strong TR2:
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{f}{\to} Y \to Z \to T X
                    \\,;
            %p
              %strong TR3:
              a triangle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %mi Z
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi h
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{f}{\to} Y \stackrel{g}{\to} Z \stackrel{h}{\to} T X
            %p is a distinguished triangle precisely if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %mi Z
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi h
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi T
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Y \stackrel{g}{\to} Z \stackrel{h}{\to} T X \stackrel{-T(f)}{\to} T Y
            %p is a distinguished triangle;
            %p
              %strong TR4:
              given two distinguished triangles
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %mi Z
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi h
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{f}{\to} Y \stackrel{g}{\to} Z \stackrel{h}{\to} T X
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ′
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo ′
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X' \stackrel{f'}{\to} Y' \stackrel{g'}{\to} Z' \stackrel{h'}{\to} T X'
            %p
              and given morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi β
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^\alpha &amp;&amp; \downarrow^\beta
                    \\\
                    X' &amp;\stackrel{f'}{\to}&amp; Y'
                    }
            %p
              there exists a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : Z \to Z'
              extending this to a morphism of distinguished triangles in that the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi β
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∃
                                  %mi γ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi T
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi α
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi g
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi h
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                    \&amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; Z
                    \&amp;\stackrel{h}{\to}&amp; T X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^\alpha &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\beta}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\exists \gamma}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{T(\alpha)}}
                    \\\
                    X' &amp;\stackrel{f'}{\to}&amp; Y'
                    \&amp;\stackrel{g'}{\to}&amp; Z'
                    \&amp;\stackrel{h'}{\to}&amp; T X'
                    }
            %p commutes;
            %p
              %strong TR5 (octahedral axiom):
              given three distinguished triangles of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                            %mi Y
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi h
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi X
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                            %mi Z
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi k
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi Y
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                            %mi T
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi g
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi f
                            %mi Z
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi l
                            %mi Z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi X
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \&amp; X \stackrel{f}{\to} Y
                    \\stackrel{h}{\to} Y/X
                    \\stackrel{}{\to} T X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; Y \stackrel{g}{\to} Z
                    \\stackrel{k}{\to} Z/Y
                    \\stackrel{}{\to} T Y
                    \\\
                    \&amp; X \stackrel{g \circ f}{\to} Z
                    \\stackrel{l}{\to} Z/X
                    \\stackrel{}{\to} T X
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p there exists a distinguished triangle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi u
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
